Sval: a panel-list takes the panel's background

panel-list.css sets its background token on `:host` from
--background-color-box, the background of a box in the page. A panel-list
floats over the page, so it takes Mozilla's token for a floating panel,
--panel-background-color, instead. Sval's pages set --background-color-box
to a translucent card colour in the dark theme, and a panel-list inside
another component's shadow tree (moz-select's) is out of reach of a page's
sheet, so the token it reads is the only place to set it from. Sval sets
--panel-background-color in sval-page.css.

diff --git a/toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.css b/toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.css
index 2d1063cf95..bccf72bdfd 100644
--- a/toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.css
+++ b/toolkit/content/widgets/panel-list/panel-list.css
@@ -22,7 +22,7 @@
 }
 
 :host {
-  --panel-list-background-color: var(--background-color-box);
+  --panel-list-background-color: var(--panel-background-color);
   --panel-list-color: var(--text-color);
   --panel-list-border-radius: var(--border-radius-small);
   --panel-list-box-shadow: var(--popup-box-shadow);
